        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 90.09,
          "en": "Thankfully, converting a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.09,
          "end": 93.05,
          "en": "to such an ObjectId object is simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.05,
          "end": 96.96000000000001,
          "en": "We just use ObjectId, what we're importing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.96000000000001,
          "end": 99.31,
          "en": "from the Mongo module here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.31,
          "end": 103.33,
          "en": "We're just using this as a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.33,
          "end": 105.97,
          "en": "and we pass our string id to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.97,
          "end": 108.093,
          "en": "and this will convert it to an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.46000000000001,
          "end": 111.58,
          "en": "Now, we'll also need to change one thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.58,
          "end": 114.7,
          "en": "ObjectId always wants a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.7,
          "end": 118.56,
          "en": "and this tid could actually be undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.56,
          "end": 120.04,
          "en": "as you see here in the tooltip.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.04,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "The reason for that is that TypeScript doesn't know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 125.77,
          "en": "with certainty whether we'll be able to find a todoId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.77,
          "end": 126.97,
          "en": "in the params.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.97,
          "end": 128.25,
          "en": "Well, since we wrote this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 128.25,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "we, of course, know there will be a todoId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 131.803,
          "en": "if this route is reached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 132.79,
          "end": 135.92,
          "en": "and, in TypeScript, we can add a exclamation mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 135.92,
          "end": 139.42000000000002,
          "en": "to really make this clear that this will never be undefined.",
